XDA_POST_YOGI.bbcode = 4804826) for the 2026-10-18 builds. Besides these, update every file name 20261013 -> 20261018
(Installation, Downloads and the grizzly section), as in earlier updates.

== 1. Build info: the firmware line (all three posts) ==
Replace:
[*]Firmware not included: you must already be on stock CD1A.261005.003 (see Requirements)
With:
[*]Firmware: the fastboot zip doesn't flash it, so you must already be on stock CD1A.261005.003 (see Requirements). Over-the-air updates include the stock firmware the build is made for.

== 2. What works (kodiak post only; append to the list) ==
[*]Over-the-air updates (Settings > System > System updates), from the 2026-10-18 build on
[*]Google's charging screensaver (Settings > Display & touch > Screen saver)

== 3. Updating (kodiak post: replace the whole "Updating" paragraph and its code block) ==
[B]Updating[/B] keeps your data.
[LIST]
[*][B]Over the air[/B] (from the 2026-10-18 build on): Settings > System > System updates finds, downloads and installs new builds, then asks you to restart. If a new build fails to boot, the phone goes back to the one you had.
[*][B]Rooted with Magisk?[/B] When the update is ready, open Magisk > Install > [I]Install to inactive slot (after OTA)[/I] instead of restarting, or root is gone (KernelSU has the same option). A custom kernel has to be flashed again after each update.
[*][B]With a computer[/B] (always works, and needed once to get from an older build to 2026-10-18):
[CODE]
adb reboot bootloader
fastboot update EvolutionX-17.0-20261018-kodiak-12.3-Unofficial-fastboot.zip
[/CODE]
[/LIST]

== 3b. Updating (cubs and yogi posts: insert after the "Installation (clean flash)" section, before Downloads) ==
[B]Updating[/B] keeps your data. From the 2026-10-18 build on, Settings > System > System updates finds, downloads and installs new builds, then asks you to restart; if a new build fails to boot, the phone goes back to the one you had. Rooted with Magisk? When the update is ready, use Magisk > Install > [I]Install to inactive slot (after OTA)[/I] instead of restarting, or root is gone. With a computer (and once, to get onto 2026-10-18 from an older build): [ICODE]fastboot update <zip>[/ICODE] from the bootloader.

== 4. Downloads (all three posts; append to the list) ==
[*]OTA packages for the updater: the zips without [ICODE]-fastboot[/ICODE] in the same SourceForge folder (not for fastboot). Update info: [URL=https://github.com/denson9874/evolution_ota]denson9874/evolution_ota[/URL]

== 5. Changelog (new first entry) ==
kodiak post:
[*][B]2026-10-18:[/B] Over-the-air updates through Settings > System > System updates. Espada kernel v3 (Linux 6.12.92) by Kevtrejo37 built in (CASS scheduler, Simple LMK, measured EM). Google's charging screensaver built in, and fixed: it showed 0% and drew the battery level too wide. Fixed a remaining brighter flash, in a lit room, when the screen times out into the always-on display. Some Google apps drew Google Sans Flex text wider than designed. kodiak and grizzly builds.
cubs post:
[*][B]2026-10-18:[/B] Over-the-air updates through Settings > System > System updates. Espada kernel v3 (Linux 6.12.92) by Kevtrejo37 built in (CASS scheduler, Simple LMK, measured EM). Google's charging screensaver built in, and fixed: it showed 0% and drew the battery level too wide. Fixed a remaining brighter flash, in a lit room, when the screen times out into the always-on display. Some Google apps drew Google Sans Flex text wider than designed.
yogi post: same as cubs (yogi remains on stock Google GKI).

